    "min_post_rule": "A truncated post-window is kept only when it still covers **75 % of the requested horizon** — 9 of 12 months, 18 of 24. The floor is a fraction rather than a month count because the two horizons are of different lengths: a rule stated in months would either admit four months as an \"h = 24\" estimate or reject a 20-month window out of 24. Every kept row carries `truncated_by_next_transition`; a window below the floor is published as `not_estimated` with its reason and the number of months it had, and is never fitted.",
    "post_end_rule": "A post-window is truncated at the next transition, so an event is never compared against months that belong to its successor. With four transitions 36 to 96 months apart, the truncated windows are the honest ones: sharing months between two events would double-count the same violence.",
