  "placebo": {
    "rule": "Every eligible month in the series is tried as if it were a transition, with the same windows, statistic and controls. The p-value is the **tail in the direction of the estimate** — for an increase, the share of placebo statistics at least as large; for a decline, the share at most as small — and it is reported per event and for the largest of the four real events, the latter because a reader looking at four estimates is looking at the largest of them whether or not the artifact says so. The p-value is the add-one randomisation form, `(1 + #{tail}) / (n + 1)`, so it is never zero: with 58 placebo months the smallest attainable value is 1/59 = 0.017, and the artifact may not claim more resolution than that.",
    "direction": "same_side_tail",
    "direction_why": "Declared as the same-side tail rather than one-sided on increase, because the headline case people ask about — the 2015 transition — is a **fall** in reported violence, and an increase-only rule would report every decline as \"no shift\" by construction. It is also not tested in absolute magnitude: the placebo null is not centred on zero (reported fatalities drift down through the window, so the placebo distribution sits near a 32 % decline), and a magnitude test against an off-centre null would score a large fall as \"easily matched\" while its own left tail says the opposite. The signed tail uses the empirical null as it actually is.",
    "p_definition": "(1 + #{placebo at least as extreme as the observed shift, on the side the shift points at}) / (n + 1)",
    "eligible_months_rule": "A month is eligible when it has `pre_months` before it and enough months after it inside the series to satisfy `min_post_fraction` at the **longest** declared horizon (18 months), and it lies more than `buffer_months` from any real transition. Requiring the strictest horizon of every placebo month keeps the placebo distribution identical across horizons, so a p-value at h = 12 and one at h = 24 are drawn from the same set. The exclusion buffer is declared so that a placebo cannot be a real transition wearing a different hat.",
