  "verdict_rule": "Per event, per outcome, at the h=12 focus horizon in the declared baseline variant: **`shift_detected`** when the per-event placebo p-value is <= 0.05 *and* the pre-trend placebo shift is smaller in magnitude than the post-window shift; **`not_interpretable_pre_trend`** when the pre-trend shift is at least as large; **`check_not_available`** when the pre-trend placebo cannot be run at all (it needs 120 months before the transition and the series is shorter behind the earliest event) — a missing check is reported as missing, not as a null; **`no_shift_detected`** otherwise. The family-wise p-value is published for every event regardless of its verdict, because four events read together are the largest of four whatever the rule says.",
